# Code owners.
#
# Everything, one owner, for now. This file's job today is to auto-request a
# review on every pull request; it sits otherwise inert.
#
# DO NOT ENABLE "Require review from Code Owners" WHILE THERE IS ONE OWNER.
#
# GitHub forbids approving your own pull request. With `* @bhavinvirani` and a
# Code Owners review requirement, every PR Bhavin opens becomes unmergeable by
# the only person allowed to merge it — a deadlock on the maintainer's own work,
# on day one, with no way out except turning the setting back off.
#
# Dependabot PRs are unaffected either way: he is not the author, so he can
# approve those.
#
# Flip it on the day a second person gets the Write role, alongside
# "require 1 approving review". That is a settings change, not a rework.
# See MAINTAINERS.md and PLAN.md §5.5.

